{
  "schema_version": 6,
  "comment": "Keyed by payload name. Each payload has one or more variants. fw_min/fw_max are hand-typed from the dev's own release notes -- never auto-parsed. author/author_url are attribution fields. source_repo is the project's primary URL; backup_url is an optional mirror/fallback location for the SAME artifact -- if you have files sourced from both, run dedupe to confirm they're byte-identical (matching SHA-256 means it's the same artifact, safe to trust either source). This isn't auto-verified yet -- core/ never fetches over the network by design, so cross-checking backup_url against source_repo is future discovery/sync-engine work, not something done automatically today. protected_fallback=true means this artifact is NEVER deleted by retention even if older/superseded. Categories use the condensed 10-category list in categories.json v3. v6: added onionHEN, ChronicLoader, PIZZA-HEN (as PIZZAHEN), kstuff-lite (as kstufflite), BackPork, ps5-webkit-autoloader, ps5-payload-manager, ftpsrv, ProsperoMgr, JailbreakStore; added itsPLK variant to elfldr; confirmed etaHEN-Zecoxao's real hosting URL. Registry keys avoid internal hyphens where the real filename's base name has none (PIZZAHEN, kstufflite, webkitautoloader, ps5payloadmanager) purely so the key reads cleanly -- resolve_identity() matches against whatever the actual filename's name_part is, so this is a naming choice, not a technical requirement. v7: fixed registry keys that didn't match real filenames -- PIZZAHEN->PIZZA-HEN, ChronicLoader->ChronicLoader-PS5-Payload, kstufflite->kstuff-lite, webkitautoloader->webkit-autoloader (split into installer/host variants), ps5payloadmanager->ps5-payload-manager. Caught by testing real filenames against resolve_identity() before shipping, not assumed correct.",
